WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.176 --> 00:00:02.543
- You know that success is something

00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:04.407
that you define for yourself,

00:00:04.407 --> 00:00:08.019
and it can't really be defined
by anybody else for you.

00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:09.369
I only want to make things that are going

00:00:09.369 --> 00:00:11.256
to reach as many people as possible.

00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:12.384
I don't believe in niche.

00:00:12.384 --> 00:00:13.797
I never want to settle.

00:00:13.797 --> 00:00:16.692
I never want to be just
happy with where I'm at.

00:00:16.692 --> 00:00:18.452
I'm just going to prove you wrong.

00:00:18.452 --> 00:00:20.660
I'd mush rather you sit there and be like,

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.738
huh, I was wrong.

00:00:21.738 --> 00:00:23.791
Anyone who's trying to tell you like,

00:00:23.791 --> 00:00:27.055
you need to gain monetary
value right now from your art,

00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:30.104
is somebody who is eating off of you.

00:00:30.104 --> 00:00:32.392
There's something really
nice about having an idea

00:00:32.392 --> 00:00:35.277
and then running into the
room and then recording it.

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:36.437
I don't want boss.

00:00:36.437 --> 00:00:37.699
I don't think we need that.

00:00:37.699 --> 00:00:38.986
This is about life.

00:00:38.986 --> 00:00:41.633
I'm trying to be real, because
the internet isn't real.

00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:43.268
I'm definitely not a rapper.

00:00:43.268 --> 00:00:44.674
I don't want to be a rapper.

00:00:44.674 --> 00:00:45.871
Rappers can only get this far.

00:00:45.871 --> 00:00:47.152
I don't want to be the guy on camera like,

00:00:47.152 --> 00:00:48.497
you should be following your dreams,

00:00:48.497 --> 00:00:49.622
and then people are like...

00:00:49.622 --> 00:00:51.306
I have five kids.

00:00:51.306 --> 00:00:52.531
- He's an American actor,
comedian, and musician.

00:00:52.531 --> 00:00:54.064
As a performing artist,
he usually performs

00:00:54.064 --> 00:00:57.963
with the stage name Childish Gambino.

00:00:57.963 --> 00:01:00.435
He was nominated for two
Grammy Awards in 2015.

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:02.511
He's Donald Glover,

00:01:02.511 --> 00:01:06.011
and here are his Top 10 Rules for Success.

00:01:07.958 --> 00:01:11.430
- Define success for yourself early.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.484
And it can change, it's okay.

00:01:14.484 --> 00:01:16.963
But just know that success is something

00:01:16.963 --> 00:01:18.940
that you define for yourself

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.905
and it can't really be defined

00:01:20.905 --> 00:01:21.738
by anybody else for you,

00:01:21.738 --> 00:01:25.905
because everybody else is
kind of full of (bleep).

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:29.905
And you know, you really
have to believe in yourself,

00:01:29.905 --> 00:01:32.818
and not in like a "believe in yourself"

00:01:32.818 --> 00:01:34.651
kind of way, but in a,

00:01:35.508 --> 00:01:37.383
know what you're getting out of it,

00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:39.208
you can't change a lot
of the things around you.

00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:42.955
And a lot of people are going
to tell you a lot of things.

00:01:42.955 --> 00:01:44.675
You have to have faith in yourself

00:01:44.675 --> 00:01:46.092
and have good friends around you.

00:01:46.092 --> 00:01:48.592
So I would just say, you know,

00:01:51.246 --> 00:01:53.236
be good to yourself.

00:01:53.236 --> 00:01:56.964
Believe in yourself, do what you want,

00:01:56.964 --> 00:01:58.921
and be cool with it, be okay.

00:01:58.921 --> 00:02:00.088
Like yourself.

00:02:01.694 --> 00:02:03.027
You should be...

00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:07.688
Nobody should ever, you
should never put out something

00:02:07.688 --> 00:02:10.393
and be like, this isn't a good whatever.

00:02:10.393 --> 00:02:13.893
I think it's whack that Macklemore's like,

00:02:15.214 --> 00:02:17.399
this album shouldn't have won,

00:02:17.399 --> 00:02:18.965
Kendrick, you should have won.

00:02:18.965 --> 00:02:20.681
That's whack.

00:02:20.681 --> 00:02:21.867
If you believe in that album,

00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:23.325
you should be like,

00:02:23.325 --> 00:02:24.390
I thought that my album was good.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.167
'Cause that's the thing.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.200
I think that my album's like the best.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.299
I love my album.

00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:29.307
I think it's dope.

00:02:29.307 --> 00:02:30.376
Like if I was a kid, I'd be like,

00:02:30.376 --> 00:02:31.668
this album's the truth.

00:02:31.668 --> 00:02:33.632
Why not like your own stuff?

00:02:33.632 --> 00:02:36.130
So yeah, like yourself.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.513
I hate niche.

00:02:37.513 --> 00:02:38.793
I'm so tied of niche.

00:02:38.793 --> 00:02:41.525
Niche is something that
I'm glad to see go away

00:02:41.525 --> 00:02:43.490
from this past decade.

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.319
It makes sense I guess like,

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:46.736
it makes sense...

00:02:50.814 --> 00:02:53.632
After the internet, that model makes sense

00:02:53.632 --> 00:02:55.111
for a lot of things, I guess.

00:02:55.111 --> 00:02:56.414
Making a niche.

00:02:56.414 --> 00:02:58.307
But I think we just need to be smarter.

00:02:58.307 --> 00:03:01.932
Making a product for only a select few,

00:03:01.932 --> 00:03:04.564
you can definitely sustain that product.

00:03:04.564 --> 00:03:07.126
But I feel like the risk that you take,

00:03:07.126 --> 00:03:11.448
that maybe it's good for
everybody, is worth it.

00:03:11.448 --> 00:03:12.871
I only want to make things

00:03:12.871 --> 00:03:15.296
that are going to reach as
many people as possible.

00:03:15.296 --> 00:03:16.335
I don't believe in niche.

00:03:16.335 --> 00:03:19.207
I think that that is a really lame way...

00:03:19.207 --> 00:03:21.563
That comes from wanting more money.

00:03:21.563 --> 00:03:22.396
- Yeah.

00:03:24.468 --> 00:03:27.180
- You know, just not even
more money, but stable money.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.063
Cause you know you can get...

00:03:29.063 --> 00:03:31.930
And I'm just, I'm not interested
in making things safe.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:35.063
- I just don't want to be
okay with where I'm at.

00:03:35.063 --> 00:03:37.149
I never want to settle.

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:40.299
I never want to be just
happy with where I'm at.

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:42.525
I always want to be going for better.

00:03:42.525 --> 00:03:45.108
(crowd cheers)

00:03:46.162 --> 00:03:46.995
I like...

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.848
I just want to always get better at stuff.

00:03:49.848 --> 00:03:50.782
Emotions are powerful.

00:03:50.782 --> 00:03:52.043
- [Interviewer] You're
not against bullying?

00:03:52.043 --> 00:03:52.876
- I'm not.

00:03:52.876 --> 00:03:53.780
- [Interviewer] What do you mean?

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.047
- I'm not against bullying,

00:03:56.047 --> 00:03:58.026
because I feel like the world is bullies.

00:03:58.026 --> 00:03:59.761
Like, there's so many people
that are going to tell you

00:03:59.761 --> 00:04:02.981
that your idea is stupid, or
that you don't belong here,

00:04:02.981 --> 00:04:04.593
or you don't deserve certain things.

00:04:04.593 --> 00:04:07.200
- [Interviewer] But wouldn't
it be a better place--

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.827
- [Donald Glover] If
people didn't do that?

00:04:08.827 --> 00:04:10.469
- [Interviewer] But you're
saying you're not against it

00:04:10.469 --> 00:04:11.821
because it's unrealistic to be against it?

00:04:11.821 --> 00:04:13.821
- I'm saying that we
probably wouldn't have

00:04:13.821 --> 00:04:16.423
Kanye West, Bill Gates, or anyone,

00:04:16.423 --> 00:04:17.904
without someone being like,

00:04:17.904 --> 00:04:19.521
you're not worth it.

00:04:19.521 --> 00:04:21.464
We wouldn't have them.

00:04:21.464 --> 00:04:24.856
We wouldn't have people who were like,

00:04:24.856 --> 00:04:26.224
no, this is worth it.

00:04:26.224 --> 00:04:29.331
Because if everybody's ideas was worth it,

00:04:29.331 --> 00:04:33.248
and they felt that way,
we'd just have nothing,

00:04:34.865 --> 00:04:36.340
everything would be the same.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.422
You need somebody to be like, I'm right.

00:04:39.422 --> 00:04:41.195
You need a Joan of Arc
to be like, I'm right,

00:04:41.195 --> 00:04:42.386
I'm right, I'm right.

00:04:42.386 --> 00:04:43.474
Even if it's crazy.

00:04:43.474 --> 00:04:44.492
Even if it's cra--

00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:45.325
And then eventually people are like,

00:04:45.325 --> 00:04:46.158
maybe they're not crazy.

00:04:46.158 --> 00:04:47.109
- [Interviewer] Are you that way?

00:04:47.109 --> 00:04:49.966
- I mean, yeah (laughs).

00:04:49.966 --> 00:04:51.339
I like to believe that.

00:04:51.339 --> 00:04:52.172
People don't--

00:04:52.172 --> 00:04:54.870
- [Interviewer] 'Cause you
seem like such a modest guy

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.870
when you're on the show.

00:04:57.755 --> 00:04:59.296
- [Donald Glover] I'm a salty dude though.

00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:00.298
- Are you?

00:05:00.298 --> 00:05:01.721
- Oh yeah, I remember everybody...

00:05:01.721 --> 00:05:03.204
I mean, I got beefs with stuff.

00:05:03.204 --> 00:05:04.787
I remember stuff...

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.274
And I'm like, most of the things I do,

00:05:07.274 --> 00:05:09.187
it's just like, no I'm right.

00:05:09.187 --> 00:05:10.771
I believe in myself.

00:05:10.771 --> 00:05:12.013
- [Interviewer] You're vengeful?

00:05:12.013 --> 00:05:13.531
- Not vengeful, I'm salty.

00:05:13.531 --> 00:05:15.535
- What's the difference?

00:05:15.535 --> 00:05:17.152
- The difference would be,

00:05:17.152 --> 00:05:18.652
vengeful would be,

00:05:20.117 --> 00:05:20.950
I'm going to come and
destroy you, I think.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:21.783
It's like, I'm going to wait around.

00:05:21.783 --> 00:05:23.784
- I'm taking your number down and I'm--

00:05:23.784 --> 00:05:25.539
- I'm coming for you.

00:05:25.539 --> 00:05:26.968
- I'm coming for you.

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:28.628
- I'm salty which means,

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:31.199
I think salty is a different thing,

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:33.621
because I'm like, I'm just
going to prove you wrong.

00:05:33.621 --> 00:05:35.453
I'd much rather you sit there and be like,

00:05:35.453 --> 00:05:36.703
huh, I was wrong.

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.439
Because I think that's growing.

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.846
There's lots of times that I've done stuff

00:05:40.846 --> 00:05:42.283
and I'm like, I was wrong about that,

00:05:42.283 --> 00:05:43.585
and I didn't even know.

00:05:43.585 --> 00:05:45.535
And it makes you look
at things differently,

00:05:45.535 --> 00:05:47.733
experiences in your life.

00:05:47.733 --> 00:05:51.624
I want to make people
think, you were wrong.

00:05:51.624 --> 00:05:53.814
- I think anybody who has control

00:05:53.814 --> 00:05:57.120
over their art should just be doing it.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.790
I made a short film,
and that was just art.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.365
I just wanted to make that.

00:06:02.365 --> 00:06:04.733
Anybody that's trying to tell you,

00:06:04.733 --> 00:06:08.192
you need to gain monetary
value right now from your art,

00:06:08.192 --> 00:06:10.970
is somebody who is eating off of you.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.387
That's the truth.

00:06:13.608 --> 00:06:16.461
Somebody who's eating off of you.

00:06:16.461 --> 00:06:18.764
But the thing is, you're
eating off of you because...

00:06:18.764 --> 00:06:21.347
I only see what I want to make.

00:06:22.401 --> 00:06:23.771
That's all I see.

00:06:23.771 --> 00:06:25.270
When people ask, do you want to do this,

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:26.267
do you want to do that,

00:06:26.267 --> 00:06:29.930
and I only see the thing
I'm supposed to make.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.498
I'm not concerned on whether or not,

00:06:31.498 --> 00:06:32.537
what's it called?

00:06:32.537 --> 00:06:34.483
Is this called painting,
or music, or whatever?

00:06:34.483 --> 00:06:37.389
Just, this is a thing
I'm supposed to make.

00:06:37.389 --> 00:06:38.639
And I go to it.

00:06:39.896 --> 00:06:43.382
So worrying about monetary value,

00:06:43.382 --> 00:06:45.559
and are people going to pay for this,

00:06:45.559 --> 00:06:47.809
is only going to ruin this.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.656
It's only going to make this
less of what I want it to be.

00:06:52.656 --> 00:06:56.323
And yeah, I don't want
to make albums or toys,

00:06:58.987 --> 00:07:01.647
I want to make concepts
that people are like,

00:07:01.647 --> 00:07:03.984
wow, this really changed...

00:07:03.984 --> 00:07:05.559
I have dreams where things

00:07:05.559 --> 00:07:07.172
are still upside down when I turn them,

00:07:07.172 --> 00:07:08.515
and I'm still trying to figure out

00:07:08.515 --> 00:07:11.654
how to do that in real life and stuff.

00:07:11.654 --> 00:07:15.091
Yeah, I just don't see the
point in cutting yourself short.

00:07:15.091 --> 00:07:16.206
And I know, it's weird...

00:07:16.206 --> 00:07:18.271
I don't think it's weird,

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:20.581
I think it's just sort of bull-(bleep)

00:07:20.581 --> 00:07:21.809
when someone's like, oh, it's pretentious

00:07:21.809 --> 00:07:24.075
to not like studios.

00:07:24.075 --> 00:07:26.566
And I was like yeah, but
I don't know any artist

00:07:26.566 --> 00:07:27.970
who really likes studios.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:29.499
Not because studios are bad places.

00:07:29.499 --> 00:07:31.436
But just because, you know,

00:07:31.436 --> 00:07:33.499
I feel like I'm wasting money there.

00:07:33.499 --> 00:07:34.921
Every time I'm not doing something,

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.325
I'm like (bleep), this
hour costs blah blah blah.

00:07:36.325 --> 00:07:38.945
There's something really nice

00:07:38.945 --> 00:07:42.264
about having an idea and
then running into the room

00:07:42.264 --> 00:07:43.187
and recording it.

00:07:43.187 --> 00:07:46.376
Not worrying about, you know, anything,

00:07:46.376 --> 00:07:47.979
other than you're hanging
with your friends.

00:07:47.979 --> 00:07:50.270
I just try to make the vibe

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:52.948
like you're making
something with your friends.

00:07:52.948 --> 00:07:55.615
The more people enjoy something,

00:07:56.768 --> 00:07:58.901
the more likely everyone else will.

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:02.591
You have a testing market in your house,

00:08:02.591 --> 00:08:05.294
when you're hanging out with
people who are like-minded.

00:08:05.294 --> 00:08:08.008
- You said you never
want to work for anyone.

00:08:08.008 --> 00:08:09.627
- Yeah, I want a boss.

00:08:09.627 --> 00:08:11.304
I don't think we need that.

00:08:11.304 --> 00:08:12.873
(crowd cheers)

00:08:12.873 --> 00:08:14.123
I really don't.

00:08:15.204 --> 00:08:17.676
I mean, we live in a time now where

00:08:17.676 --> 00:08:20.582
it's easier now than ever to do anything.

00:08:20.582 --> 00:08:21.675
I don't understand...

00:08:21.675 --> 00:08:22.760
People come up to me like,

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.364
how do I start making a movie?

00:08:24.364 --> 00:08:26.183
I was just like, you got a phone.

00:08:26.183 --> 00:08:29.021
If I had a phone when I was like seven

00:08:29.021 --> 00:08:31.593
I would have made every
movie I ever thought.

00:08:31.593 --> 00:08:33.398
I just would be doing it all the time.

00:08:33.398 --> 00:08:35.034
There's a lot of like, there's the thing.

00:08:35.034 --> 00:08:38.678
We're fighting for, I'm
fighting for right now...

00:08:38.678 --> 00:08:40.517
I'm not doing this in music.

00:08:40.517 --> 00:08:41.537
This is not about rap.

00:08:41.537 --> 00:08:42.533
I'm an artist.

00:08:42.533 --> 00:08:43.746
This is about life.

00:08:43.746 --> 00:08:44.911
I'm trying to be real.

00:08:44.911 --> 00:08:46.449
Because the internet isn't real.

00:08:46.449 --> 00:08:47.578
There's so much (bleep)
that happens online,

00:08:47.578 --> 00:08:48.937
and people perceive it
and it's packaged as real.

00:08:48.937 --> 00:08:52.033
But nothing's real any more.

00:08:52.033 --> 00:08:53.747
- My man, my man--

00:08:53.747 --> 00:08:54.895
- That's the reason, people are like,

00:08:54.895 --> 00:08:58.130
Donald looks awkward, or
there's a mistake here,

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:00.240
and I'm like yeah, cause it's real.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.484
I'm constantly trying to be real.

00:09:01.484 --> 00:09:02.588
So that's the thing.

00:09:02.588 --> 00:09:03.507
If I don't say something--

00:09:03.507 --> 00:09:04.340
- Oh, Donald looks awkward?

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:05.173
I got news for you.

00:09:05.173 --> 00:09:06.006
Guess what?

00:09:06.006 --> 00:09:07.025
Donald is awkward.

00:09:07.025 --> 00:09:07.858
That's why I'm here--

00:09:07.858 --> 00:09:08.933
- But that's the thing, I am though,

00:09:08.933 --> 00:09:10.122
and that's what makes me me--

00:09:10.122 --> 00:09:11.183
- [Interviewer] 100%.

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:12.438
- And you got to deal with it.

00:09:12.438 --> 00:09:13.700
So it's like, I'm not...

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:14.808
And also, I'm not worried.

00:09:14.808 --> 00:09:15.954
I can figure it out.

00:09:15.954 --> 00:09:17.105
I'm not a dummy.

00:09:17.105 --> 00:09:19.098
And I stand up for what I believe in.

00:09:19.098 --> 00:09:21.176
And it's not about
hiphop, it's about life.

00:09:21.176 --> 00:09:23.038
This is real.

00:09:23.038 --> 00:09:24.098
I represent real.

00:09:24.098 --> 00:09:25.494
I'm trying to do real stuff.

00:09:25.494 --> 00:09:27.474
I sort of feel like,

00:09:27.474 --> 00:09:28.480
I've said this before,

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.862
I've listened to Kanye
interviews and he's like

00:09:30.862 --> 00:09:32.603
I can't go any farther.

00:09:32.603 --> 00:09:36.586
I used to be like, I want to be a rapper.

00:09:36.586 --> 00:09:39.122
I'm trying to be a rapper
and just do all this stuff.

00:09:39.122 --> 00:09:40.926
And I was like, I realized,

00:09:40.926 --> 00:09:43.721
yo, that's my superpower,
I'm not a rapper.

00:09:43.721 --> 00:09:44.554
I'm definitely not a rapper.

00:09:44.554 --> 00:09:45.686
I don't want to be a rapper.

00:09:45.686 --> 00:09:47.908
Rappers can only get this far.

00:09:47.908 --> 00:09:49.884
They can only go so far.

00:09:49.884 --> 00:09:51.846
And I want, this is a gift,

00:09:51.846 --> 00:09:53.523
I get to make this show.

00:09:53.523 --> 00:09:55.162
It's something that
nobody else gets to make,

00:09:55.162 --> 00:09:56.947
and make it weird and personal,

00:09:56.947 --> 00:10:00.614
and something that they
would let, probably,

00:10:01.992 --> 00:10:03.466
they wouldn't let Schoolboy Q do it.

00:10:03.466 --> 00:10:06.806
Even though he's probably
got crazy, dope ideas.

00:10:06.806 --> 00:10:09.306
I think this is my superpower.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:11.850
I want to like...

00:10:12.727 --> 00:10:14.894
I want to do something dope.

00:10:16.023 --> 00:10:18.973
I guess the worst thing that
could happen to me right now,

00:10:18.973 --> 00:10:22.934
would be if I just couldn't
make things anymore.

00:10:22.934 --> 00:10:25.500
That there wasn't an
outlet, and be honest.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.978
I think the one thing I'm thankful for

00:10:27.978 --> 00:10:31.080
is that I can still change stuff.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:34.735
I can still do things differently.

00:10:34.735 --> 00:10:37.372
I meant that, when I
wrote that in Instagram.

00:10:37.372 --> 00:10:38.691
You can always be better.

00:10:38.691 --> 00:10:41.242
I seriously meant that.

00:10:41.242 --> 00:10:44.847
So I guess I'm very
thankful that, you know,

00:10:44.847 --> 00:10:47.018
things aren't always
over till they're over.

00:10:47.018 --> 00:10:48.670
'Cause no one feels
like they're good enough

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:49.920
- Yeah.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.461
- Nobody, we we all, how old are you?

00:10:52.461 --> 00:10:53.294
- 29.

00:10:54.685 --> 00:10:57.033
- Yeah, we're all around that age

00:10:57.033 --> 00:11:00.200
where it was like, jobs weren't there

00:11:01.634 --> 00:11:03.445
after they came out, and
the people would just...

00:11:03.445 --> 00:11:05.079
That's when I feel like I'm being lied to.

00:11:05.079 --> 00:11:07.376
Cause everyone kind of became
a freelance photographer,

00:11:07.376 --> 00:11:09.558
freelance...everybody
became a freelance...

00:11:09.558 --> 00:11:12.867
And then you realize, oh
man, no one's really happy.

00:11:12.867 --> 00:11:13.931
(laughs)

00:11:13.931 --> 00:11:18.089
No one's really happy
because we're not attaining

00:11:18.089 --> 00:11:20.012
those goals that people...

00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:22.271
You're supposed to have kids
and do all these things,

00:11:22.271 --> 00:11:23.347
that we're supposed to...

00:11:23.347 --> 00:11:24.474
And no one's really happy

00:11:24.474 --> 00:11:26.384
because they realize all those things

00:11:26.384 --> 00:11:28.264
are kind of not what make you happy.

00:11:28.264 --> 00:11:31.386
That's what our parents
did, to have purpose.

00:11:31.386 --> 00:11:33.979
And now we have all that stuff.

00:11:33.979 --> 00:11:36.366
And the thing we're supposed to do

00:11:36.366 --> 00:11:37.592
is really be helping each other,

00:11:37.592 --> 00:11:39.896
but we've been brought up in this kind of

00:11:39.896 --> 00:11:42.425
well, I'm supposed to be
the top-ranking manager

00:11:42.425 --> 00:11:44.988
at this point, and have...

00:11:44.988 --> 00:11:46.563
And it's not real.

00:11:46.563 --> 00:11:47.623
It's just not real.

00:11:47.623 --> 00:11:49.250
It's not necessary.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.093
Everybody should just be
following their passion.

00:11:51.093 --> 00:11:53.384
'Cause they're going to
be good at that, at most.

00:11:53.384 --> 00:11:57.532
But people are too
worried about their jobs.

00:11:57.532 --> 00:11:58.873
'Cause people got to eat.

00:11:58.873 --> 00:12:01.280
It's not sad, but it's true.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.609
But people got to eat, and I feel bad.

00:12:03.609 --> 00:12:05.286
Like I don't want to be
the guy on-camera like,

00:12:05.286 --> 00:12:07.092
you should be following your dreams

00:12:07.092 --> 00:12:10.729
and people are like, I
have five kids (laughs),

00:12:10.729 --> 00:12:12.062
I can't do that.

00:12:13.119 --> 00:12:15.698
But I think it's true,
and people are scared

00:12:15.698 --> 00:12:18.412
and vulnerable because
it's dangerous to do that.

00:12:18.412 --> 00:12:21.638
But I don't think we're
going to grow, if we don't

00:12:21.638 --> 00:12:22.766
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:12:22.766 --> 00:12:26.083
I made this video because
John Huang asked me to.

00:12:26.083 --> 00:12:27.408
So if there' a famous entrepreneur

00:12:27.408 --> 00:12:29.205
